Bootstrap: docker
From: nvcr.io/nvidia/blueprint/rag-frontend:2.3.0

%help
    NVIDIA RAG Blueprint Frontend
    Official image: nvcr.io/nvidia/blueprint/rag-frontend:2.3.0

    Node.js server that serves the React UI and acts as a reverse proxy
    to the RAG Server and Ingestor Server backends.

    In Singularity (shared host network) the server binds to port 3000.
    Docker maps it to 8090 externally, but in Singularity there is no
    port mapping — access the UI at http://<compute-node-IP>:3000.

    The backend URLs are read at runtime from environment variables:
      VITE_API_CHAT_URL  — RAG Server base URL  (default: http://rag-server:8081/v1)
      VITE_API_VDB_URL   — Ingestor Server URL  (default: http://ingestor-server:8082/v1)

    In Singularity set both to localhost since all services share the host network:
      singularity run \
        --env VITE_API_CHAT_URL=http://localhost:8081/v1 \
        --env VITE_API_VDB_URL=http://localhost:8082/v1 \
        rag-frontend.sif

%labels
    Author NVIDIA RAG Blueprint - Singularity Deployment
    Version 2.3.0
    Description React frontend with Node.js reverse proxy for RAG Blueprint
